d 'PKGTRANSFER': module to rebuild an installed package setup on another machine, online or offline
d
d  pkgtransfer transfers the user-written packages installed in one
d Stata installation to another. It reads stata.trk in the current
d PLUS directory to identify installed packages and their sources,
d including SSC, personal websites, and GitHub, and writes a
d do-file of the ssc install, net install, and github install
d commands needed to reinstall them online on a new machine.
d Alternatively, download(online) downloads every package file from
d its source, or download(local) copies it from the local PLUS
d directory, and builds a local installation script and a ZIP
d archive for offline installation, and the restore option restores
d the online source URLs in stata.trk after an offline install.
d Options restrict or exclude packages, choose the target operating
d system for plugin filtering, name the generated do-file and ZIP
d archive, and allow existing output to be overwritten. The output
d records package sources, not a snapshot of package versions.
d Results returned in r() include the number and list of packages
d processed, the download mode, the target operating system, and
d the names of the generated do-file and ZIP archive. 
d
d KW: package management
d KW: installation
d KW: reinstall
d KW: migration
d KW: offline installation
d KW: stata.trk
d KW: SSC
d KW: GitHub
d KW: net install
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261030
d
d Author: Timothy P Copeland, Karolinska Institutet
d Support: email timothy.copeland@@ki.se
d
f pkgtransfer.ado
f pkgtransfer.sthlp
